" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></summary><div><a href="/nyc/brooklyn/">Brooklyn</a><a href="/nyc/manhattan/">Manhattan</a><a href="/nyc/brooklyn/#williamsburg">Williamsburg &amp; DUMBO</a><a href="/nyc/manhattan/#midtown">Midtown &amp; Chelsea</a></div></details><a href="/nyc/projects/">Projects</a><a href="/nyc/about/">About</a><a href="/nyc/resources/">Resources</a></nav><a class="btn primary header-quote" href="/nyc/contact/">Request a quote <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><details class="export-mobile"><summary>Menu</summary><nav><a href="/nyc/">Home</a><a href="/nyc/products/">Products</a><a href="/nyc/interior-signs/">Interior Signs</a><a href="/nyc/exterior-signs/">Exterior Signs</a><a href="/nyc/vehicle-wraps/">Vehicle Wraps</a><a href="/nyc/custom-signs/">Custom Signs</a><a href="/nyc/trade-show-displays/">Trade Show Displays</a><a href="/nyc/retractable-banners/">Retractable Banners</a><a href="/nyc/brooklyn/">Brooklyn</a><a href="/nyc/manhattan/">Manhattan</a><a href="/nyc/projects/">Projects</a><a href="/nyc/gallery/">Gallery</a><a href="/nyc/resources/">Resources</a><a href="/nyc/contact/">Contact</a></nav></details></div></header><div class="product-ribbon"><div class="wrap"><a href="/nyc/interior-signs/">Interior signs</a><a href="/nyc/exterior-signs/">Exterior signs</a><a href="/nyc/vehicle-wraps/">Vehicle wraps</a><a href="/nyc/custom-signs/">Custom signs</a><a href="/nyc/trade-show-displays/">Trade show displays</a><a href="/nyc/retractable-banners/">Retractable banners</a></div></div><main><section class="wrap product-hero"><div><p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/nyc/">New York</a> / Signs for Manhattan workplaces and storefronts</p><p class="eyebrow">VISION GRAPHICS · NEW YORK</p><h1>Signs for Manhattan workplaces and storefronts</h1><p class="lead">A Manhattan signage project often needs to fit into a busy building as well as a busy street. Reception areas, glass partitions, shared entrances and compact storefronts each call for a different balance of identity and information. Vision Graphics can help organize the design, production and site details into a clear project scope. Share the project ZIP, photos and building requirements so the design can respond to the actual space. Manhattan is an initial service focus, with coverage, access and delivery or installation arrangements confirmed project by project.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="#request-quote">Discuss your project <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a class="text-link" href="#options">Explore options <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></div><figure class="project-image product-photo"><img src="/nyc/assets/mcs-new-service-custom-signs-960.webp" srcset="/nyc/assets/mcs-new-service-custom-signs-480.webp 480w, /nyc/assets/mcs-new-service-custom-signs-960.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 50vw" alt="Signage example related to Signs for Manhattan workplaces and storefronts" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Illustrative sign example · Michigan Custom Signs source</figcaption></figure></section><section class="wrap section article-layout"><article><section><h2>Office identity that works within the building</h2><p>A lobby logo may be only the beginning of an office move or refresh. Room signs, meeting-room privacy, tenant directories and directions should use the same naming and visual system. Collect the property’s sign criteria and coordinate approval with facilities or management before the artwork is finalized.</p></section><section id="midtown"><h2>Midtown: plan around the office and building</h2><p>For a Midtown office move or refresh, connect reception branding with meeting-room privacy, room identification and directions from the shared entrance. Ask the property team which sign criteria, delivery procedures and work hours apply. Share the floor plan, approved room names and photos of proposed mounting surfaces. Identify the signs needed for first occupancy separately from later enhancements.</p></section><section id="chelsea"><h2>Chelsea: consider the visitor’s full approach</h2><p>For a Chelsea shop, studio, gallery or hospitality space, look at the journey from the sidewalk to the point of service. Should the window introduce the business, promote an event or keep the interior visible? Would a lobby logo or wall graphic help confirm arrival? Include changing displays, landlord requirements and access arrangements so permanent and temporary graphics can be scoped together.</p></section><section><h2>Plan for access and the customer’s view</h2><p>For a storefront, consider how pedestrians see the sign from the sidewalk and what the window reveals about the business. For an upper-floor office, consider the journey from shared entrance to suite door. Delivery windows, elevators, access restrictions and wall conditions can affect the project and should be discussed early.</p></section><section><h2>Include building coordination in the brief</h2><p>For a Manhattan office, retail space or restaurant, the project brief should include the building as well as the graphics. Share photos, dimensions, the address and your desired completion date. Include the property manager's requirements, available work hours and any known delivery or access restrictions. These details help define the proposed installation scope alongside material and design choices. Vision Graphics can review reception signs, window graphics and other project needs, then confirm responsibilities, access arrangements and timing for the specific location.</p></section><section><h2>What affects a Manhattan project quote</h2><p>Sign dimensions, materials, quantities and artwork preparation determine much of the production scope. Mounting height, surface condition, old-sign removal, delivery arrangements and restricted work hours can affect site work. Confirm who coordinates the building and who performs each installation task. For projects in the Financial District, Flatiron, SoHo or another neighborhood, the actual property requirements and confirmed service coverage determine the plan.</p></section><section id="options"><p class="eyebrow">MATERIALS &amp; APPROACHES</p><h2>Find the right fit.</h2><div class="options-grid"><div><h3>Reception and office branding</h3><p>Coordinate dimensional logos, glass privacy and room information. Review the floor plan, wall finishes and building sign criteria together.</p></div><div><h3>Retail and hospitality graphics</h3><p>Connect storefront identity, window messaging and interior graphics. Distinguish enduring business information from promotions that change.</p></div><div><h3>Directories and wayfinding</h3><p>Organize shared entrances, tenant information and routes to suites or service points. Confirm the names and locations before artwork approval.</p></div><div><h3>Event and portable displays</h3><p>Plan retractable banners, printed displays and event graphics around the available space, venue requirements and reuse needs.</p></div></div></section><section><h2>Where it can work</h2><ul class="check-list"><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Office moves and tenant refreshes</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Reception and conference-room branding</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Retail and hospitality interiors</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Managed commercial properties</li><li><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-check" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path></svg>Studio, gallery and business-event displays</li></ul></section><section class="faqs"><h2>A few useful answers.</h2><details><summary>Can you coordinate with a property manager?<span>+</span></summary><p>Include the property’s requirements and approval contacts in the project discussion so responsibilities can be defined.</p></details><details><summary>Is Manhattan installation automatically included?<span>+</span></summary><p>No. Access, installation capability and scope must be confirmed for the particular location and product.</p></details><details><summary>What building information should we provide?<span>+</span></summary><p>Share the property manager's sign criteria, approved work hours and any known delivery, elevator or access requirements. Include the building contact when appropriate. We will review these details and clarify responsibilities before agreeing on the installation scope.</p></details><details><summary>Can we plan graphics around an office move or store opening?<span>+</span></summary><p>Yes. Share your target date and identify the graphics needed first. Tell us when the space will be accessible and when artwork and building decisions can be approved. We can review those dependencies and confirm a project schedule; timing depends on the final scope and approvals.</p></details></section></article><aside class="product-aside"><p class="eyebrow">LET’S START WITH THE DETAILS</p><h3>Have a space in mind?</h3><p>A photo, a few measurements and your project ZIP help us ask the right questions.</p><a href="/nyc/contact/?photo=1" class="btn dark"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="17" height="17" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-camera" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13.997 4a2 2 0 0 1 1.76 1.05l.486.9A2 2 0 0 0 18.003 7H20a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V9a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h1.997a2 2 0 0 0 1.759-1.048l.489-.904A2 2 0 0 1 10.004 4z"></path><circle cx="12" cy="13" r="3"></circle></svg> Send a project photo</a><hr><h3>Related possibilities</h3><a href="/nyc/office-signs/">Office signs<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="15" height="15" viewbox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-up-right" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 7h10v10"></path><path d="M7 17 17 7"></path></svg></a><a href="/nyc/lobby-sig